course: dictionary
lesson: 1043
title: Bored: a feeling and a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bored is a feeling. You feel bored when nothing interesting is happening and you have nothing to do, like on a long car ride or a rainy day. The context shows which meaning fits: «A bored pet can become unhappy and destructive» is about how an animal feels.
explain: Bored can also be the past form of the verb bore. To bore is to make a hole by drilling, or to make someone feel bored. Look at the words around it: «The long talk bored the whole class yesterday» uses the verb, while «He sat and watched, bored and guilty» uses the feeling.
explain: Saying «I'm bored» politely is fine, but «You're boring» can be unkind, because it blames the other person. Bored can also be strong, as in «bored stiff» or «bored to tears», which both mean very bored. When you meet bored, swap in tired and restless and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Bored means tired and restless because nothing interesting is happening or you have nothing to do.
fact: «Bored stiff» and «bored to tears» both mean very bored.
fact: Bored is also the past form of «bore»: to make a hole by drilling, or to make someone feel bored.
fact: Being bored can lead to new ideas, like inventing a game, reading or drawing.
fact: In Mandarin, «wúliáo» (WOO-lyow) is the word for bored, and both of its tones rise.
exercise: «He sat and watched, bored and guilty, while his team ran one runner short.» What does bored mean here? | Very loud | Excited about the game | Drilled through | *Tired and restless, with nothing interesting to do
exercise: Which sentence uses bored as the past form of the verb bore? | «A bored pet can become unhappy.» | «Many injuries happen when children are bored.» | *«The long talk bored the whole class yesterday.» | «He sat and watched, bored and guilty.»
exercise: Which is a polite way to tell someone you feel bored? | You're boring | Stop talking, you bore me | *I'm bored, can we do something new? | Your game is rubbish
test: «A bored pet can become unhappy and destructive.» What does bored mean in this sentence? | Asleep in the sun | Very happy and busy | Drilled into the wall | *Tired and restless with nothing to do
test: What do toys, play, walks and new things to sniff do for a bored pet? | Teach it to drill holes | *Keep it happy | Make it bored | Make it cross
exam: Which statement about bored is true? | Bored always means very excited | Bored is always a rude word | Bored only means something you use to drill | *Bored can be a feeling, or the past form of the verb bore
